 "title": "GTA 6 is 30 FPS even on PS5 Pro. Fine, or a dealbreaker?",
 "audio": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3Lh3gaSoJDsjYAzqFyj65XamsxE/hf_20261114_053421_7793b80e-9756-4f9d-94a8-bc66d7f4acc6.wav",
 "script": "Even on PS5 Pro, GTA 6 targets 30 frames per second. Rockstar confirmed it on November 10, and no 60 mode is announced. Note it says targeting, not locked. The Pro does get sharper upscaling and ray traced shadows. Rockstar says it's keeping the full density and detail of Leonida. Some fans call 30 a dealbreaker. Others note no modern Rockstar game has launched at 60, and that Starfield got savaged for 30 too. Is 30 fine for a world this detailed, or a dealbreaker for you? Comment your side.",
